              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7e3222bd-d9dc-41cd-9ace-a2234dd32b34</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">THE ZONE-CELL CHECK

TestPollutantCanyonContainerE2E's first-tier
assertion reads OpenFOAM's own self-reporting.
After Run &gt; Create Zones and Run &gt; Simulate,
look in the solver log (Parse Case Logs, or
run_01_foamRun.txt) for:

  - selecting cells using cellZone
  - selected N cell(s) with volume ...

N MUST BE NONZERO. "- selected 0 cell(s) with
volume 0" is the silent empty-zone plume: every
dictionary parses, the solver reaches End, a
tracer field is written, and the concentration
is zero everywhere.

Also check the log does NOT contain
  Model &lt;x&gt; defined for field &lt;y&gt; but never used
which means the fvModel's sources key and the
function object's field disagree.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>2450</X>
